{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"Recommendations were timing out, and they work again. I submitted the mitigation to the conductor endpoint, which accepted it.\n\nI never found out why the old recommendation pod was unreachable. The `recommendation` deployment had been pinned to `kind-worker` with a `nodeSelector`, and `frontend` was pinned to `kind-worker2`. Requests to `/api/recommendations` through the frontend proxy returned 504 after 15 seconds. A TCP connection from a pod on `kind-worker2` to the recommendation service failed. Connections to other services on the same node worked, such as product-catalog on `kind-worker`.\n\nI removed the `nodeSelector` from both deployments, and the scheduler moved the new pods to `kind-worker3`. After that, `/api/recommendations` returned 200 in about 25 ms, and `/api/products` and `/` also returned 200. I only re-tested through the frontend proxy and did not watch it for a sustained period.\n\nThe flagd flags were all off, so they weren't the cause."}}
